Quarantine::hold again replaces an item already held under the same batch id
instead of joining it: the join that c9f5fbc (Join an item already held under
a batch id) put at the top of hold is removed, which restores the plain insert
that came before. An item revert returns into an id held meanwhile then
replaces the entries held there, while the version index still names them
under the id. DESIGN.md §8.2, "a batch id names one review item".

Since drafts 52 and 53's failed-report rules no seed fails with this
patch (0 to 9,999, and 0 to 499 at 2,000 steps, with fetch corruption on), so the pinned
seed is gone and the rule's unit tests below stand in for it.

test: delocal-engine quarantine::tests::holding_under_an_existing_id_joins_the_item
test: delocal-engine quarantine::tests::an_item_returned_by_revert_joins_the_item_holding_its_id

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs b/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs
index 619b8dd..363fce1 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/quarantine.rs
@@ -222,13 +222,6 @@ impl Quarantine {
     /// then leave those versions behind, and a later version dominating one
     /// of them would join an item that no longer exists and be lost.
     pub fn hold(&mut self, item: HeldItem) {
-        if self.items.contains_key(&item.batch) {
-            let batch = item.batch;
-            for entry in item.entries.into_values() {
-                self.join(batch, entry);
-            }
-            return;
-        }
         for entry in item.entries.values() {
             self.record(&entry.path, entry.version.clone(), entry.stamp, item.batch);
         }
